WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.080
A mug of tea sits on a desk
in a room at twenty degrees.

2
00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:07.220
Fresh from the kettle,
it reads ninety degrees.

3
00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:09.510
Ten minutes later, sixty.

4
00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:12.310
That's thirty degrees in ten minutes.

5
00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:15.400
So three degrees a minute, every minute?

6
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:18.650
If so, when would the
tea reach forty degrees?

7
00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:21.860
And is steady cooling
even the right picture?

8
00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:25.130
In this mission, you'll use
Newton's law of cooling,

9
00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:29.790
a model where the excess temperature
above the room decays exponentially.

10
00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:33.820
You'll see why the curve levels
off at twenty degrees, not zero.

11
00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:38.880
And you'll take a natural log to find the
decay constant from just two readings.

12
00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:42.680
Your mission: work out when
the tea will be forty degrees.
